### Adding a .gitignore File                                 {#sec:gitignore}

First, to avoid checking in lots of emphemeral build files, add a file called
`.gitignore` to the top level of your repository, containing:

```
.pio
.vscode
build
```

To do this from the command line try something like this:
```bash
cd com3505-student-2024
cat <<EOF >.gitignore
.pio
.vscode
build
EOF
git add .gitignore
git commit -vm 'added a .gitignore file'
git push
```

From now on files or directories like `.pio` (PlatformIO's build tree) will
not be added to the repo or listed in git status requests.


